        "original_id": "4ba8231a-945e-56c0-a1b1-96219d491f01",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Whit Alexander, Richard Tait, Karen Seyfarth, Andreas Seyfarth, Gary Baseman\n- Products: Cranium, Thurn and Taxis, Teacher's Pet\n- Companies: Hans im Glück, Rio Grande Games, ABC, Disney\n- Topics: board games, party games, game design, publishing\n\nFacts:\n- In 1998, Whit Alexander and Richard Tait created Cranium as a party game after Richard Tait spent a weekend playing games with another family and recognized a need for a game involving a variety of skills.\n- In 2006, Karen Seyfarth and Andreas Seyfarth designed the board game Thurn and Taxis.\n- In 2006, Hans im Glück published Thurn and Taxis in German as Thurn und Taxis, and Rio Grande Games published it in English.\n- Gary Baseman created the Emmy-winning ABC and Disney cartoon series Teacher's Pet.\n- Gary Baseman was the artistic designer of Cranium, which is described as a popular award-winning board game.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
